w: Mild He lays His glo- ry by, * Born that man no more may die. *
w: Now dis- play Thy sav- ing po- wer, Ruin- ed na- ture now re- store; *
w: Let us Thee, though lost, re- gain, * Thee, the Life, the in- ner man: *
